.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=Preview Plugin

@Contents
$ #Preview Plugin#
 Fast, native image viewer with hardware-accelerated decoding
and terminal graphics support for far2l.

   ~Overview & Features~@Overview@
   ~Opening Images~@Opening@
   ~Navigation~@Navigation@
   ~Zoom & Scaling~@Zoom@
   ~Panning & Dragging~@Pan@
   ~Rotation & Mirroring~@Rotation@
   ~File Selection & Tagging~@Selection@
   ~Configuration & Settings~@Preview@
   ~Supported Formats~@Formats@
   ~Troubleshooting & FAQ~@Troubleshooting@

@Overview
$ #Overview & Features#
 The Preview plugin provides seamless image viewing inside far2l
both in GUI mode and inside supported terminal emulators.

 Key features:
   - Zero-delay image browsing with background async prefetch
   - Native OS hardware-accelerated decoders (Apple ImageIO on
     macOS, GdkPixbuf on Linux)
   - Built-in fallback decoders for WebP, HEIC/AVIF, TIFF, etc.
   - QuickView panel preview (#Ctrl+Q#)
   - Terminal graphics: far2l GUI, Kitty, iTerm2, and Sixel
   - Smooth zooming, panning, 90° & fine 1° rotation, mirroring
   - Fast native video storyboards (3×3 contact sheets with timecode badges)
   - Far2l panel selection synchronization (mark files in viewer,
     batch copy/move/delete on exit)

 ~Contents~@Contents@

@Opening
$ #Opening Images#
 There are multiple ways to open images with the Preview plugin:

   #F3#             If "Override built-in F3 viewer" is enabled,
                    pressing F3 on an image file opens Preview.
   #Enter#          If "Open with Enter" is enabled, pressing Enter
                    opens the image in Preview.
   #Ctrl+PgDn#      If "Open with Ctrl+PgDn" is enabled, opens
                    the image directly.
   #Ctrl+Q#         QuickView: shows live preview in inactive panel.
   #F11#            Plugins menu -> select #Preview#.
   #preview:<path># Type in far2l command line to open specific file.
   #Enter# / #O#    Inside viewer: open image in default system app.

 ~Contents~@Contents@

@Navigation
$ #Navigation#
 Switch between images in the current directory:

   #Right# / #Down#    Next image in folder
   #Left# / #Up#       Previous image in folder
   #Home#              First image in folder (when not rotated)
   #End#               Last image in folder (when not rotated)
   #PgDn# / #PgUp#     Next / Previous image (if not bound to zoom)

 Background prefetching automatically decodes adjacent images
in a worker thread, ensuring instantaneous (0 ms) flipping.

 ~Contents~@Contents@

@Zoom
$ #Zoom & Scaling#
 Adjust zoom level and viewport fit:

   #PgUp# / #+# / #Num+#     Zoom in
   #PgDn# / #-# / #Num-#     Zoom out
   #Shift+PgUp#              Fine zoom in (+1%)
   #Shift+PgDn#              Fine zoom out (-1%)
   #*# / #A#                 Auto-fit to window / panel
   #/# / #Z#                 100% (original 1:1 pixel size)
   #S#                       Cycle fit modes (Auto -> Width -> Height -> 100%)
   #=# / #Num5#              Reset zoom and pan offsets
   #Mouse Wheel#             Smooth zoom in / out

 ~Contents~@Contents@

@Pan
$ #Panning & Dragging#
 Move around within zoomed-in images:

   #Alt+Arrows#              Pan image viewport
   #Alt+Shift+Arrows#        Fine pan (1 pixel per press)
   #Mouse Left Drag#         Click and drag to pan interactively

 ~Contents~@Contents@

@Rotation
$ #Rotation & Mirroring#
 Rotate and flip images on the fly:

   #Home#                    Rotate 90° counter-clockwise
   #End#                     Rotate 90° clockwise
   #Shift+Home#              Fine rotate 1° counter-clockwise
   #Shift+End#               Fine rotate 1° clockwise
   #Tab#                     Rotate 90° clockwise
   #Shift+Tab#               Rotate 90° counter-clockwise
   #F7# / #H#                Mirror horizontally
   #F8# / #V#                Mirror vertically
   #Mouse Right Click#       Rotate image clockwise

 Images with EXIF orientation metadata are automatically rotated
upright upon loading (configurable in settings).

 ~Contents~@Contents@

@Selection
$ #File Selection & Tagging#
 Select images directly in the viewer for subsequent batch operations:

   #Ins#                     Toggle selection of current file
   #Space#                   Select file and advance to next image
   #Backspace#               Deselect file and go back to previous
   #Esc# / #F10#             Close viewer (all selections are preserved
                             on the far2l panel)

 Use this workflow to quickly cull photos or review albums, then
press #F5# (Copy), #F6# (Move), or #F8# (Delete) on the panel.

 ~Contents~@Contents@

@Preview
$ #Configuration & Settings#
 Press #F9# in the viewer or open #F11# -> #Options# -> #Preview#:

   #Enable plugin#           Enable or disable preview functionality
   #Apply EXIF orientation#  Auto-rotate based on EXIF tag
   #Open with Enter#         Intercept Enter key on image files
   #Open with Ctrl+PgDn#     Open viewer on Ctrl+PgDn
   #Show in QuickView#       Display image in QuickView panel (Ctrl+Q)
   #Override built-in F3#    Use Preview when pressing F3
   #Auto-fit after rotate#   Recalculate fit after 90° rotation
   #Fast transforms#         Use fast integer scaling
   #Compact frame#           Minimal window frame border
   #Use OS image codec#      Use hardware-accelerated system decoder
   #Default fit mode#        Auto, Fit Width, Fit Height, 100%
   #Image masks#             Space-separated wildcard extensions

 ~Contents~@Contents@

@Config
$ #Configuration & Settings#
  See ~Configuration & Settings~@Preview@.

 ~Contents~@Contents@

@Formats
$ #Supported Formats#
 The plugin supports a wide range of image formats:

   - #JPEG# (.jpg, .jpeg) with EXIF orientation
   - #PNG# (.png) with 8-bit, 16-bit, and alpha channel
   - #GIF# (.gif) static and animated
   - #WebP# (.webp) lossy, lossless, and alpha
   - #HEIC / HEIF / AVIF# (.heic, .heif) via libheif / ImageIO
   - #TIFF# (.tif, .tiff) multi-page and uncompressed/compressed
   - #BMP#, #TGA#, #PSD#, #HDR#, #ICO#
   - #Video files# (.mp4, .mkv, .mov, .avi, .webm, .m4v, etc.)

 For video files, the plugin automatically generates a 3x3 contact
sheet (storyboard) with timecode badges, giving an instant visual
summary of the entire film. Press #Enter# or #O# to open the video
in the system's default media player.

 On macOS, Apple ImageIO and AVFoundation provide hardware-accelerated
decode for images and video storyboards.
 On Linux, GdkPixbuf, native modular libraries, and FFmpeg provide
fast decoding with graceful fallbacks.

 ~Contents~@Contents@

@Troubleshooting
$ #Troubleshooting & FAQ#
 #Terminal lacks graphics support#
   The running terminal emulator does not support Kitty, iTerm2,
   or Sixel graphics protocols. Run far2l in GUI mode or use a
   supported terminal (e.g. Kitty, Ghostty, iTerm2, WezTerm, Foot).

 #Image does not open on Enter or F3#
   Check #F9# settings: make sure "Override built-in F3 viewer"
   or "Open with Enter" is checked, and verify that the file
   extension is listed in "Image masks".

 #Large images take time to load#
   Ensure "Use OS image codec" is enabled. On macOS, ImageIO
   automatically downsamples huge photos directly during decoding.

 #Selections lost#
   Selections made with #Ins#, #Space#, and #Backspace# are applied
   to the active panel upon exiting with #Esc# or #F10#.

 ~Contents~@Contents@
